    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17552" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔτ-ανδρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>together with the men, men and all,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς αὐτάνδρους ἀπέβαλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					1.23.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. Sosyl.<i><span class="en">
				p.31
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.582
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Bacch.</u>
				3
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεις αὐ. ἀνῃρῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					7.60
				</span></i>
			: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔ. λαός</span> the
			people, <i>every man of them,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				3.7.31
			</span></i>.</div>
